.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- scp with colon-path local names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I source
\&...
.I target
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path aware wrapper around
.BR scp (1).
By default (when
.B COLON_WRAP
is unset), a built-in rewrite implementation handles local colon-path
arguments and delegates to
.B cp
for local copies.
Set
.B COLON_WRAP=1
to invoke
.B scp
from
.B PATH
(including remote
.I host:path
forms).
.PP
Colon-path rewriting applies to local
.B BASE:LEAF
arguments (when
.I BASE
contains
.BR / ).
Forms like
.I host:path
(no slash before
.BR : )
are left unchanged for scp.
.PP
Destination directory placement follows the same
.I DEST/LEAF
rules as
.BR colon-cp (1)
for local destinations.
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the rewritten command without executing it.
When using the built-in rewrite (default), output is prefixed with
.BR (rewrite) .
.TP
.B \-3
Route through the local host on both ends.
.TP
.B \-4
Force IPv4 addresses only.
.TP
.B \-6
Force IPv6 addresses only.
.TP
.B \-A
Forward agent authentication.
.TP
.B \-C
Enable compression.
.TP
.B \-O
Use legacy scp protocol.
.TP
.B \-p
Preserve modification times, modes, and xattrs.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode.
.TP
.B \-r
Recursively copy directories.
.TP
.B \-T
Disable strict filename checking.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose mode.
.TP
.BR \-c " " I CIPHER
Select cipher.
.TP
.BR \-F " " I ssh_config
Specify alternate ssh_config file.
.TP
.BR \-i " " I identity_file
Select identity (private key) file.
.TP
.BR \-J " " I destination
Jump host for ProxyJump.
.TP
.BR \-l " " I limit
Limit bandwidth (Kbit/s).
.TP
.BR \-o " " I ssh_option
Pass ssh_option to ssh.
.TP
.BR \-P " " I port
Specify port (note uppercase P).
.TP
.BR \-S " " I program
Specify remote shell program.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLON_WRAP
When unset (default), use the built-in rewrite implementation (local only;
remote
.I host:path
requires external scp).
When set to
.BR 1 ,
exec the stem of
.B $0
from
.B PATH
(\fBcolon-scp\fR → \fBscp\fR).
When set to a program name, exec that program instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scp (1),
.BR colon-rsync (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
